{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested — DESIGN ONLY, authority revision 27 at 1f3cfca5e3cf72c01ccf94721d5111c672dd8a9b, tree 32e18197774504acf4310077e95bccbc2452a85f. All three filed artifacts examined, primary first; evidence for eee603c6c0deb57d4cd7b7b18502a5382535c941. No implementation closure or adoption.\n\nP2 — Record a retry mint safely after an older read finalizes its receipt (primary 11204, 11207, 11429, 11470, 11486–11488, 11663, 11679–11685). A receipt remains owed after its original three write attempts have unknown outcomes, with the deciding read still pending. The current resend-receipt guard permits a rightful admin to add branch room and open a new receipt operation, attempt and mint: every old WRITE attempt has an outcome; no guard waits for the old deciding read. Before the new mint answers, that old read can observe the expected receipt commit and set the receipt written, hence final. It gives the new attempt no outcome. The new mint then confirms; its own attempt still has no outcome and the publication is not aborting, so generic mint selects receipt.token assignment. That changes an item already final before this entry. The adopted R19 every-effect invariant (5745) and outcome-output rule EJ11 (3801), freshly read, make this a rule fault: no entry and the confirmed mint reply stays offered. This is legal serialized design input, not a concurrent transaction or a measured runtime failure. New branch room was admitted; capacity exhaustion is not the cause.\n\nMake mint outcomes aware of the terminal receipt target, recording truthful own evidence and required cleanup without changing final receipt slots. Preserve already admitted attempts, unknown duties, actual credential provenance and original mint/write holder. In the reverse order, new mint before old read, the shared receipt.token can name the branch-held retry mint while the old read is publication-held: reconcile revoke-inherits-mint-holder with the general own-outcome-holder rule and its next-judge-only exception. This is a cleanup ownership conflict to resolve with the same repair, not a proven numeric overflow. Keep the control where a late mint follows its OWN attempt's outcome: that already takes the safe revoke arm and is not this defect. Cover both serial orders. Do not invent another attempt's outcome, fabricate not-sent evidence, drop pending work or block recovery forever behind an unknown read.\n\nP2 — Name and retain selected reports required by the planner (section 6.5, 7811–7919; section 13.17 question 3, 14712). The current reserve fields and count 2+v+2j omit selected report entries. The note expressly says their commits are in no entry at hand, G does not fetch them, and check 2 relies on runtime ancestry evidence. Effective planner assertion 53ecfb42 answer (c), personally FULL inspected, requires reserve to name each selected report, up to 32 more entries, so judgment and replay derive the report-to-commit binding from retained verified entries. Add the bounded typed facts, bind them exactly to manifest selections, fetch/retain at delivery, copy the origin uses and derive commits from those entries on replay. Reconcile the fields/count/refusal controls, R2 send duty, evidence/custody and all carried restatements. This is design conformance; no forged result admitted by an unbuilt runtime is claimed.\n\nState the revised foreign-entry ceiling and duplicate/source policy explicitly. Within the existing 128 ceiling, added reports reduce admissible verdict/job combinations; the current size estimate already counts 128 uses records. Adding up to 32 reports does not by itself prove 160 uses or overflow. The 248629-byte sum includes a guessed 16384-byte header/effects/update allowance; its 13515-byte margin is not a complete static bound. Recalculate the full entry and retained-input bounds for the final forms. Planner accepts the interim 64-verdict limit, 65-author/eight-key bounds and visible reserve refusal at 65 owed receipts. These decisions do not prove capacity in all five dimensions.\n\nArchitecture: retained observation rows, explicit origin uses, typed verdict/job facts and the separate receipt item improve the design; terminal receipt state and outstanding credential/attempt lifetimes must remain distinct. Security: preserve controller independence, verified source facts, truthful outside-effect identity and cleanup under the proper holder. Simplification: use the existing named-fact retention path for reports and one explicit terminal-target mint/cleanup policy instead of hidden runtime knowledge or final-item exceptions. Missing object-format input for an outside first-head constructor and unchecked Git vectors remain interface/implementation duties; absent/failed seen can be dispatched before hash comparison, so no unconditional hashing P2 is promoted.\n\nFour independent readers freshly personally FULL read all assigned current body and complete U3 intervals. Collective coverage: all three complete bodies 1786178 bytes/19321 LF; complete adopted-R26-to-head U3s 270876 bytes/2710 LF; complete exact-parent-to-head U3s 127324 bytes/1088 LF, including both zero facts deltas. Sixteen units, 251 actual assigned displays; native nine captures, all part/slice proofs and nine unions passed. Checker personally FULL read all four reports and ledgers, three complete counterreports/ledgers and the size supplement ledger; personally read complete receipt/first-head and generic mint contexts plus current reserve fields/size and adopted R19 final/fault excerpts. Twelve supplemental parts and 26 countercheck slices verified. No personal FULL claim for the 1.34 MB primary or 350 KB corrections. No gaps or display deviations.\n\nSeal /tmp/artroom-checker-r27-1f3c-ordinary-root-binding.json, 40388 bytes, SHA256 d68514b94cdff4557d6d51e075e1e83fc7656231aa6cb2d3bd3107223a56cbf8. No tests/gates/project execution/evaluators/simulations/generated histories/commit vectors/private diagnostics/provider probes/source changes. Producer counts and vectors are not checker execution credit. R19 contract and R26 authority remain in force; R23 is in review. Full I3/IA/task/application/authority/source/runtime/retention/custody/provider and all-five-capacity acceptance remain owed; estimates close no functionality.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0834cda8dbfbdd3b88543fc96b298c4399ecd729","binding":"evidence-only","head":"1f3cfca5e3cf72c01ccf94721d5111c672dd8a9b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2960327a5bf0dcd8a05ca042aa425785619dfb7a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4bb220bb86c919777f3c88f483cfeb3103eacdd8","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}